  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mallikarjun Gurulingappa Chandkawate vs The State Of Maharashtra on 14 July, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai 2023:Bhc-As:19503 38_ba_1624_2023.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1624 Of 2023 Mallikarjun Gurulingappa ...Applicant Chandkawate Versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent ... Mr. Amit A. Karande for the Applicant. Mr. R.M. Pethe, App for the Respondent-State. Coram: Smt. Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated: 14th July, 2023. P. C. :- 1. This is an application under Section 439 of the Cr.P.C. filed by the aforesaid Applicant, who is arrested in C.R. No.370 of 2023 registered with Pandharpur (city) Police Station, Solapur, for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 r/w 34 of the Ipc and Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv), 27(3)(e), 30(2)(a) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "3. The case of the prosecution is that a vehicle bearing registration No. MH-13 DQ-1402 was intercepted near Laxmanrao Patil Temple at Pandharpur city. Gutkha and Pan Masala, prohibited food items, which were being transported by the said vehicle were seized and the co-accused- Pravin Bhosale and Sandeep Pise were taken into custody. The co-accused informed the Investigating Mallikarjun Gurulingappa Chandkawate vs The State Of Maharashtra on 14 July, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/18393707/ 1 Officer that they had purchased the said prohibited food items from Karnataka. It is alleged that the Applicant is the Vendor, who had sold the said prohibited food items to the co-accused.",
    "arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the Applicant states that apart from the statement of the co-accused, there is no other material to indicate that the Applicant had sold the said prohibited food items. It is also stated that there is no prohibition in the State of Karnataka for sale of such food items.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the Applicant states that apart from the statement of the co-accused, there is no other material to indicate that the Applicant had sold the said prohibited food items. It is also stated that there is no prohibition in the State of Karnataka for sale of such food items.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
